      "id": "source-3",
      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T12:54:00Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and call trace, Comptroller oracle getter, PriceOracleProxy deployment and exploit-time bytecode, runtime disassembly, constructor-initialized baseOracle pointer, the commit-pinned reproduction, and Blueberry's post-mortem. The exploit repeatedly executes getUnderlyingPrice(address) at 0x16d43cac32329ec286dc14431e0c0e805e6f5174. Its 453-byte direct runtime resolves the bToken underlying, calls getPrice(address) on CoreOracle proxy 0xdfe469ace05c3d0d4461439e6cf5d0f46f33ec56, and returns the uniformly 18-decimal value unchanged. That missing lending-market normalization is the executable defect. The adapter has no delegatecall, selfdestruct, or state-changing entry point; deployment transaction 0xbc46bb...967f is its complete code-history anchor."
    },
